  "mn149:10.8": "The four establishings of mindfulness, the four right exertions, the four bases of power, the five faculties, the five strengths, the seven factors for awakening, and the noble eightfold path are termed the Wings to awakening <i>(bodhi-pakkhiya-dhamma).</i> <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dn16'>DN 16</a> reports that toward the end of his life, the Buddha recommended these qualities as the essence of his teaching. See <i>The Wings to awakening</i> for more details.",
